WEBVTT

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.720
Let's go back, Shadow!

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.270
It's too dangerous trawling on a day like this!

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:45.190
They're doing a nice show at the Piccadilly!

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:47.060
I bought two tickets for it!

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:59.450
Gina, run the boat towards that ship!

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:18.850
Get closer! Run the boat along the ship's side!

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:20.560
Huh? Fine.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:43.660
What the-?!

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:46.790
Was it lightning?

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:48.580
What's wrong?

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.670
The radar mast is wrecked!

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:54.960
Our communication functions are shot!

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:56.970
We can't even send an emergency signal!

00:01:57.470 --> 00:01:59.340
Okay, everybody listen up!

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:04.100
Right now, we're taking over this here ship.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.400
All right, let's go back!

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:14.780
Gina!

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:18.400
Do you <i>want</i>  to go back to prison?!

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:24.370
Just last night you woke up screaming after dreaming of those concrete walls closing in on you!

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:29.420
And now... you're getting involved in this again?

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.250
You also brought this with you?

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.040
Hey, stop that!

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.750
I've had it!

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:39.720
I've been through hell without you, and now that you're out you go and do this again?

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.970
Shut up, willya?!

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:44.760
Try wrapping your head around what
$100,000 easy money will mean to us!

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.720
I don't want to know!

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:52.560
What... is this?

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:20.880
Hey, come on!

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:22.260
Help me out!

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:23.300
Hey!

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.260
Hey, ain't that Shadow?

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.890
Bomber, slow down the boat to a near standstill!

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.730
Hey, someone throw the guy a float!

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:40.900
I walk unsteadily on paths to nowhere

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:45.030
wondering what I should do right now.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:51.500
I play the song you like on the car stereo

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:56.040
with the volume up and my feelings crystallized

00:03:56.040 --> 00:04:01.670
driving on streets with no crossroads or signals

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:07.100
with a speed that will catch up with you.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:11.560
So faraway - let's run!

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:17.860
And let's not bother with the breaks - full throttle.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:22.150
Oh someday - one of these days

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:27.240
You'll be at my place where nobody can find you.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:33.330
Whenever you suffer a breakdown one can't see

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:38.920
depend on me for your repairs.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:43.300
So faraway - let's run!

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:49.510
We'll reset and start again - even at our limit.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:53.810
Oh someday - one of these days

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:59.860
If I'm with you we'll find our dream.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:17.210
Today's the 24th, 6:30 AM. Hurricane Sharon, which has made another landfall on the Florida peninsula

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:23.510
currently has a wind speed of 112 mph and a barometric pressure of 28.11.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.880
Also, Hurricane Sharon is currently en route-

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:41.190
...it is predicted to drop to a Category Two status at around 9:00 AM.

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:44.780
It will pick up strength again once it pulls back into the Atlantic.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:47.280
Right now it is a Category Three storm.

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:52.740
Hurricane Sharon shares the same features with Hurricane Lucy from three years ago...

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:56.500
On top of the crap we have to deal with, we get this!

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:57.710
No kidding.

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:01.840
I know it's a bit early, but we gotta ship out.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:05.260
I'll take in the particulars in the car.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:13.640
A 26,000 ton tanker out of New York Harbor loaded with crude called the <i>DEXY</i>

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:17.730
was headed for Liverpool when it got hijacked.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:23.320
The <i>DEXY</i>  is right now heading south on the Atlantic.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:29.280
They're holding 20-odd crew members hostage, so we can't cowboy our way through this one.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:33.950
The suspects are after the crude oil on the <i>DEXY</i>.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:41.290
We figured the only way to take back the <i>DEXY</i>  is to put a bullet through every one of those culprits.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:48.300
If the <i>DEXY</i>  manages to pull out of American waters, we can no longer lay a finger on them.

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:53.300
And once that happens, the hostages will be as good as dead since they won't be needed any more.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:57.310
Which means we're requesting the services of that guy, right? But...

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:59.600
...is he really coming?

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:01.940
A guy like Golgo 13...

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.030
He's a man who never goes back on his word.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.910
Five minutes till the allotted time.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:23.500
Christ, can he pick a worse place to rendezvous?

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:33.260
Golgo 13 is able to stay alive for so long only because he's this overcautious.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.560
But he's meeting with <i>us</i>.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:41.940
There's no discussing this at a hotel lobby.

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:49.360
Besides, if he does have enemies lurking around here, he has nowhere to hide.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:55.780
So... you're saying he's checking us out from somewhere even as we speak?

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:57.620
Probably so.

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:11.590
Right on time.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:23.310
Who'd ever think that you'll appear from out of those fierce waves?

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:26.900
Get in. We'll have our conversation out at sea.

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:29.030
You take the controls.

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:31.400
Uh, right.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:49.880
As you can see, the <i>DEXY</i>  was boarded by an armed gang.

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:56.180
We've confirmed that three of the culprits work for the mafia boss, Whiskey Joe.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:00.350
That's Whiskey Joe.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:05.310
The main culprit is Whiskey Joe's right-
hand man who people call Bomber.

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:09.360
Those are his muscles, Louie and Bob.

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:11.280
Then there's one more.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:14.360
He's a freelance sharpshooter who goes by the name of Shadow.

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:19.370
Whiskey Joe hired him just for this hijacking.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:24.120
He's a top-notch sniper whose skills earned him a commendation from the Marines.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:29.040
This guy has such a short fuse it's a pain in the ass.

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:32.090
He's capable of pulling anything if we make a wrong move.

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:40.810
Attention <i>DEXY</i>  hijackers!

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:43.140
Immediately throw down your weapons and surren-!

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:54.690
You've gather a lot of information in such short notice.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:58.160
Shadow's lady friend became our pigeon.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:03.160
I swear, I just don't understand women.

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:09.290
She wanted us to save Shadow in return for all the dirt she knew.

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:13.630
Here, use this.

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:17.760
A Springfield M14.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:19.840
I got it from the captain's cabin.

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:22.050
What about the ship's crew?

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:23.890
Locked up in a cabin.

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:29.060
They were shaking in their boots when we
threatened to sink this ship with dynamite.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:30.810
We got a destroyer!

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:42.780
So we're facing the Navy. Guess it's all over.

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:43.870
Shut up!

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:46.830
We got a bellyful of hostages, remember?

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:48.370
Get the captain here.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:16.650
This is just a taste!

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:19.860
If you don't back off, everyone gets killed!

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:26.540
We won't stop till the last person hangs!

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:29.910
Look!

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:32.540
The destroyer's retreating!

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:34.960
Hah! How you like them apples!

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:45.050
Here's the $3 million we're paying you.

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:49.310
I'll answer once I take a look at the <i>DEXY</i>.

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:50.430
Switch places.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:14.380
If we get any closer, we'll fall within his ideal range!

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:17.840
What are you doing, Golgo 13?

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:22.380
Hey, you there! Don't get close, it's too dangerous! Get back!

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.700
This is too much!

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:48.780
It's like you're begging them to shoot you!

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:50.870
Golgo 13!

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:11.930
What the... hell...?

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:12.890
Bulletproof glass?

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:22.360
Even from a rocking ship traveling at high speeds, he was able to shoot on target.

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:23.900
He's a pro.

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:26.490
And he's no ordinary pro either.

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:28.320
Looks like it.

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:33.500
So will you accept, Mr. Golgo 13?

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:38.920
Get the <i>DEXY</i> 's blueprints and find out about the guns they're using.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:42.590
I want to know what they're carrying.

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:45.220
Sure... so you're doing it?

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:06.610
With the same intensity as before

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:12.410
Hurricane Sharon is slowly continuing east through the Florida peninsula at 21 mph.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:18.500
The barometric pressure at the eye is 28.05 with wind speeds clocking as high as 134 mph.

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:24.710
We warn all ships cruising the area to watch out for large waves.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:30.180
Also, there will be active storm clouds covering
every area due to the hurricane, plus heavy rain-

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:40.690
Is something wrong?

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:48.610
Hmph. Always on time, Golgo 13.

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:50.200
Where's the <i>DEXY</i>?

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:56.700
It's now right off Florida, 33 degrees north, 73 degrees west

00:14:56.700 --> 00:15:00.120
heading south-southwest at around 12 knots.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:04.130
They'll be outside American waters in about 2 hours.

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:07.420
The Coast Guard has the <i>Jayhawk</i> ready for you.

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:08.720
Got it.

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:28.320
All right, that's good!

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:33.030
Hmm?

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:35.830
Your timing is perfect!

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:42.750
It's no German U-boat, but it can go up to 9 knots underwater.

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:48.050
Still, what are you planning to
do with this underwater vessel?

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:50.760
Right, I forgot.

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:52.340
Here's the rest.

00:15:59.060 --> 00:15:59.770
Like you said.

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:08.780
Golgo 13 you say?

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:17.280
I can't comprehend why you'd want to entrust this job to that mystery man, Mr. Flanagan.

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:24.120
I've already selected 10 expert marksmen from the local Coast Guard.

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:26.790
We've organized sniper teams.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:34.090
As you can see, the rifles these boys are holding are equipped with PVS-14 night-vision sights.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:39.350
That means they can sense the infrared rays the culprits are emitting even in the dark.

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:41.810
Those things are capable of thermographic imagery.

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:46.230
The sniping team are on board the two ships we launched.

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:49.320
They'll close in on the <i>DEXY</i>  and shoot the bad guys.

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:55.860
The <i>DEXY</i>  will soon be 500 meters ahead.

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:59.830
Are you sure about this, Mr. Duke Togo?

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:04.460
Lower the equipment and leave this place immediately.

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:05.830
Okay.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:14.510
Wait, Mr. Kimmel

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:21.010
What I'm worried about is your
teams' confidence in their accuracy.

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:23.850
I know that you boys are excellent.

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:33.110
Still, how many times have you taken a shot in
choppy waters from a boat that's shaking like a leaf?

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:34.990
Never, not once.

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:40.990
So, you still believe you can take down a bad guy in one shot?

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:44.160
That's something I won't know unless I try.

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:10.810
What we're dealing with are thugs who killed the ship's captain in cold blood after merely seeing a destroyer.

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:16.700
If we're not 100 percent certain we'll succeed, we simply can't go off half-cocked.

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:23.080
So where in God's name did <i>you</i>  get
your confidence in this Golgo 13 guy?

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:29.460
At the very least, he may be the only person in
the world who has a 100 percent accuracy rate.

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:33.710
We got an incoming from the <i>Seahawk</i>  destroyer.

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:39.090
At 0030 hours, the <i>DEXY</i>  taking route 370

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:42.640
suffered a minor yet sudden explosion followed by a slowdown in speed.

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:45.470
The sounds of the engines and propellers have ceased.

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:49.730
That's Golgo 13.

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:52.110
The man has made his move.

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.420
Attention hijackers!

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:14.880
You got nowhere to run!

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:17.630
Throw down your weapons and surrender immediately!

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:22.140
I repeat... throw down your weapons and surrender immediately!

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:24.640
No good! The machinery is shot!

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:27.680
This ship ain't moving!

00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:31.060
Does this mean we got no choice but to surrender?

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:34.020
Shut up! We still have our hostages!

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:37.690
We'll use them to demand escape boats!

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:52.330
Bob, bring out the folks we got in the bridge!

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:55.790
If this ship can't move, then they're useless to us!

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:56.590
You got it!

00:19:57.380 --> 00:19:59.170
Louie, go with him!

00:19:59.170 --> 00:19:59.970
Right!

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:06.680
Cease your useless resistance and surrender immediately!

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:09.470
I repeat, surrender immediately!

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:16.270
All right guys!

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:18.570
W-What...?

00:20:23.530 --> 00:20:24.450
Bomber...

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:29.910
They only got our guys.

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:34.000
And each was shot once either in the head or the heart.

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:49.350
You got nowhere to run!

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:51.390
Now surrender immediately!

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:55.350
I repeat... surrender immediately!

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:56.560
Fuck with me, willya?

00:20:58.270 --> 00:21:00.320
Dammit, where are those guys?!

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:02.530
They must have given up.

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:38.270
Who the hell are you?

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:43.190
The most difficult target to shoot is the one that's falling down.

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:51.200
And you came down to shoot after calling
me out and getting me to raise my muzzle.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:56.670
So you also know how to exploit a sharpshooter's worst blind spot?

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:02.550
So... will you tell me your name?

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:07.220
Golgo... 13.

00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:45.760
I enjoyed the little things.

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:52.970
I loved when you gave me a flower every day

00:22:53.720 --> 00:22:59.060
instead of just one big bouquet

00:22:59.770 --> 00:23:03.900
of flowers.

00:23:05.980 --> 00:23:11.530
It was like a romance novel.

00:23:12.160 --> 00:23:16.120
Surely someday... just kidding.

00:23:16.450 --> 00:23:19.500
I had a dream.

00:23:19.870 --> 00:23:25.210
Your face shined eternally.

00:23:26.050 --> 00:23:31.800
Because I think of you all the time.

00:23:32.220 --> 00:23:37.350
I'm sorry, but on a lonely night like this

00:23:38.310 --> 00:23:43.860
I'm remembering you, but

00:23:44.150 --> 00:23:48.440
I won't cry like I did that day.

00:23:50.200 --> 00:23:51.610
I won't.

00:24:02.500 --> 00:24:05.170
This job will take place in mid-air.

00:24:05.170 --> 00:24:10.050
Golgo and his employer, Earp
head for their target in a small jet.

00:24:10.050 --> 00:24:16.640
At the same time, a man who detests Earp has secretly planned a murder plot of his own.

00:24:17.220 --> 00:24:21.060
The two murderous intents will bring
about crises neither party knows about.

00:24:21.850 --> 00:24:25.610
Next time on Golgo 13: Murderous Crosspoints.

00:24:22.190 --> 00:24:27.320
Murderous Crosspoints

00:24:25.610 --> 00:24:29.570
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
